course: dictionary
lesson: 11288
title: Wrongly: not correct, or unfair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Wrongly» tells you how something was done. Look inside the word: wrong, with -ly added. So wrongly means in a wrong way.
explain: A sum can be done wrongly, which means not correct. A person can also be wrongly blamed, which means blamed unfairly, when they did not do it. «Back injuries from lifting wrongly can take weeks or months to heal» means lifting in a way that was not correct.
explain: To check your meaning, swap «wrong» in for «wrongly» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Wrongly means in a way that is not correct, or by mistake.
fact: «Wrongly spelled» means the spelling is not right.
fact: «Wrongly accused» or «wrongly blamed» means someone is blamed unfairly, even though they did not do it.
fact: «The Hubble Space Telescope, launched in 1990, orbits above the air, but its mirror was wrongly shaped and astronauts fixed it in 1993.» Here wrongly means shaped in a way that was not correct.
exercise: «If someone's name is said wrongly, you gently give the right name.» What does said wrongly mean? | Said again and again | *Said in a way that is not correct | Said very loudly and clearly | Said with a big smile
exercise: «Back injuries from lifting wrongly can take weeks or months to heal.» Which meaning fits best? | Lifting something very heavy with a friend | Lifting for a long time without a rest | Lifting high above the head | *Lifting in a way that is not correct
exercise: «When we are worried, the brain fills gaps with the worst story.» Which word in this sentence shows the worst story is not checked? | gaps | worried | *worst | brain
test: Sam was wrongly blamed for breaking the window. What does wrongly mean here? | *Unfairly, when Sam did not do it | Very carefully, so the glass did not break | Loudly, in front of the whole class | Quickly, before anyone could see
test: «Her name was spelled wrongly on the card.» What does spelled wrongly mean? | Spelled out loud for everyone to hear | Spelled very neatly and clearly | *Spelled in a way that is not correct | Spelled in a fancy writing style
exam: «“Paranoid” means wrongly sure people are against you.» Which word is closest in meaning to wrongly here? | Happily | Quietly | *Mistakenly | Slowly
